<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "Require current ordinary construction evidence, proof and published exact scoped grant before source edits. Require exclusive ownership of shared CLI write scopes. Domain handlers, locks, receipt validators, recovery draft, provider policies and schedulers are read-only except the separately required USF-1195 integration validation process cleanup repair; that exception permits only bounded owned-process/stdio settlement and its focused regressions. The separately required shared binding-declaration reader extraction may move the existing pure Linear binding parser into graph source and reuse it in no-effect context interrogation; dispatch, attempts, receipts, supersession admission, locks and provider behavior remain unchanged. The separately required completion-evidence canonical preparation may extract the existing no-persistence evidence producer and delegate both interfaces to it; all proof, publication and persistence handlers retain their guards. Mutation transition mappings remain explicitly unmapped until separately admitted. The separately required no-change non-destructive replay repair may modify only materialiseNoChangeCandidate and focused regressions to authenticate and reuse exact existing state, preserve/refuse partial or conflicting existing state, and leave all other candidate operations, locks and publication semantics unchanged. The separately required candidate content digest repair may share candidate identity canonicalization between resolver and realisation, treating validated write content as opaque while preserving metadata/path guards and all previously accepted digests; generic provider digest and provider Contribution identity remain unchanged. Resolver errors retain their existing typed classification. The separately required canonical no-change execution extension may share the existing transition kernel across explicitly admitted observation and candidate-workspace effects, separate command-result and produced-artifact schema validation, export the existing native no-change producer with closed request validation, and add canonical CLI delegation and focused tests. It must not change native candidate identity, locks, creation/cleanup/replay semantics, provider behavior, proof, publication or completion authority. Effect admission requires exact compiled rule and recovery-case compatibility; graph declarations alone remain insufficient. The separately required canonical checked-receipt reuse currentness repair may modify src/commands/check.ts and focused regressions to share exact current validation-claim projection between receipt production and read authentication, compare authenticated current candidate facts and complete runtime authority dependency paths/bytes, and reject self-consistently rehashed stale claims before reuse. It must preserve receipt schema and digest domain, native execution, locks, persistence/recovery and integration-specific authority checks. It grants no new check adapter, semantic completion or parallel authority. The separately required root-derived selective check adapter has the additional bounded exception specified in the separate construction constraint." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
