<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-record-alternatives:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-record-alternatives:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A record may declare two to sixteen recordAlternative identities instead of ordinary fields. Alternatives must be distinct declared non-union records in the same schema, with distinct source types. The union declares exactly one discriminatorProperty. Every alternative requires that scalar text property with one unique allowedValue tag; all tags must be distinct. Refuse mixed fields and alternatives, missing or recursive references, nested unions, ambiguous tags and source types, or absent discriminator semantics. Derive oneOf references to the closed alternative records. Record projection requires the union source type and exactly one alternative source type on the subject, then uses that alternative's ordinary reader and field derivations. Source typing selects a structural variant, never operational authority." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:requires> <urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-record-alternatives:1> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
