<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-parallel-assessment-boundary:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Parallel safety cannot be inferred from DAG topology, a declared proved tag, empty conflicts, structural schema validity or execution success. A future assessment evaluator must authenticate exact transition members and pair denominator, semantic/currentness basis, read/write and non-file resource scopes, shared authority and ownership, provider/account concurrency, Linear serialization, evidence/recovery dependencies, conflicts and proof obligations. Unproven, blocked and proved are separate assessment variants; only current independently authenticated complete assessments may report proved. Semantic completeness and execution authority remain independent. Until the evaluator and typed assessment records are admitted, report unproven and do not admit parallel effects." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
