<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-input:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Canonical intended request contains only rootIdentity and manifestPath. Derive unique work/contract/profile through the shared context resolver, then derive the exact work packet, current immutable basis and graph-selected no-change completion policy. Candidate digest, workspace, policy, basis, profile and work overrides refuse. The canonical --input adapter may delegate only to the shared native no-change producer after exact compiled admission; the legacy explicit parser remains a compatibility interface. A binding root is refused until separately implemented, never guessed." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
