<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-safety:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The native candidate lock serializes the same derived identity only. No disjoint-scope, shared-authority, provider/resource or cross-transition parallel-safety proof is implemented here. Topological independence never admits parallel execution." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CliFieldDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:rule:no-change-descriptor-replay:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A fresh absent workspace may be created after current authority authentication. If interrupted before any workspace effect, absence must be observed again before retry. If effect completed but acknowledgement was lost, restart reauthenticates and reuses the exact complete workspace. Abrupt partial creation, unsafe/missing manifest, conflicting bytes, stale relevant basis or unknown state refuse without deleting retained state. Caught fresh-creation errors use existing bounded cleanup, which is not crash atomicity or power-loss durability. No partial-workspace repair or automatic outcome assumption is admitted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
