<urn:usf:requirement:checked-receipt-reuse-currentness:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before enabling zero-execution check receipt reuse, the canonical read accessor must authenticate the exact current validation authority claims, candidate identity/facts and complete non-candidate runtime authority dependency set, not merely self-consistent hashes or the existence of current validation. Share the producer's current validation field projection rather than maintain a second hand-authored expected receipt. Preserve read-only absence as null and all malformed, unsafe, temporary, conflicting and stale refusals. Tests must take a genuine passing receipt, independently alter command/environment/mode/resource/tool/schema/dependency claims, recompute its internal hashes, and prove typed refusal without execution, repair or mutation; unchanged genuine receipts remain readable. Preserve the existing receipt schema/digest domain and native locks/execution/persistence/recovery. Integration retains its separately derived integration-authority authentication. This requirement does not admit the future root-only check-receipts adapter or establish terminal completion or parallel safety." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
