<urn:usf:requirement:root-derived-selective-checks:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "USF-1192 requires one root-derived selective check adapter over the existing semantic kernel. Derive exact no-change identity without materialisation, complete current completionValidationObligations and existing receipt state. Authenticate every retained required member before any execution. Under the existing candidate lock, reauthenticate current-or-absent immediately before selecting execution; reuse current members and run only safely absent members. Reauthenticate the full required set after asynchronous work, refusing basis or denominator movement. Keep stable set identity separate from invocation observations and preserve scalar receipt schema and digest domains. Tests must cover genuine current reuse with zero execution, missing-only execution, concurrent duplicate prevention, stale rehashed receipts, unknown/unsafe/partial publication, restart and native refusal without state repair. A partial receipt set never establishes completion; absent CLI recovery remains explicitly unimplemented. No separate lock, scheduler, workflow sequence, provider contact or completion authority is introduced." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
