<urn:usf:requirement:completion-check-receipts-canonical-adapter:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "USF-1192 acceptance requirement: native selective-check implementation derives current completionValidationObligations, authenticates all existing members before any absent-member execution, and uses an extracted ensure-current-or-run-absent primitive under the existing candidate lock to reread each member immediately before invocation. It shares the producer's exact receipt accessor and check body, invokes only authenticated absent members, and makes concurrent canonical callers reuse a current member rather than duplicate execution. Then rederive and refuse on any currentness movement before full-set readback. For this graph-generated result fragment, transition inspection must use the existing generated descriptor schema as a dependency and construct a closed validator with $ref equal to record schemaIdentity plus schemaFragment and $id equal to this result schema resource; it must require emitted schema to equal that same IRI, and re-read/rederive before acknowledgement. No copied result schema file, caller override, execution/reuse classification, scalar receipt schema/digest change, unsafe temporary or partial recovery, completion, terminal closure, parallel safety, provider, or Linear authority follows." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
