<urn:usf:requirement:completion-check-receipts-execution-intent:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Both native check entrypoints, including legacy explicit runGraphDerivedCheck, acquire the existing candidate lock and interrogate a retained intent at intentPath before receipt cleanup or child invocation. When no intent exists, an authenticated current receipt may be reused with zero execution; no historical intent is invented. A valid retained PREPARED is pre-effect only and may proceed through STARTED. A retained STARTED with an authenticated matching receipt may settle without a child. A retained STARTED without that receipt becomes UNKNOWN and refuses without a child; UNKNOWN never retries. A retained intent publication at intentPath.pending is authenticated and reconciled or preserving-refused, never treated as absent. Existing receiptPath.pending publication is first recovered or preserving-refused by the native receipt rule, never treated as receipt absence. Malformed, stale, conflicting, unsafe or mismatched intent, pending intent or receipt preserves bytes and refuses. No known-failed typed outcome record is introduced: after a STARTED record lacks an authenticated matching receipt, including after failure or interruption, recovery remains UNKNOWN and blocked." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
