<urn:usf:requirement:selective-check-currentness-composition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Preserve exact native authentication while composing selective checks. Before execution-view creation authenticate the whole candidate, raw manifest, current basis and complete candidate facts. After view construction, rederive the same semantic basis through existing shared core derivation, compare authenticated raw manifest and complete candidate facts, and rederive validation, execution authority and intent before PREPARED/STARTED or spawn. Never weaken the ordinary workspace inventory guard to admit execution scratch. Complete-set snapshots must use one existing candidate lock: share the existing authenticated no-change reader through a callback whose entire observation runs inside that lock, preserving the public reader and all authentication. Never reacquire the same non-reentrant lock inside its callback. Regression obligations include real interruption/replay, pre-spawn manifest or basis drift with zero child execution, retained-set missing-only execution and currentness refusal through the native typed reasonCode." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required selective-check currentness composition repair may extract the unchanged native authenticated no-change workspace reader into a callback-under-existing-candidate-lock boundary in src/realisation/index.ts and delegate its existing public reader without changing its validation, identity or lock implementation. The complete-set reader in src/commands/work-completion.ts must use that boundary rather than nested lock acquisition. In src/commands/check.ts, pre-spawn reauthentication may use existing shared semantic basis derivation plus exact authenticated raw manifest and complete candidate-fact snapshots after execution-view construction, without calling or weakening the ordinary whole-workspace inventory reader while its owned scratch exists. Focused genuine interruption, drift and complete-set tests may change in the already declared test paths. No new lock policy, scratch exemption, receipt schema, controller, provider, completion or parallel authority is admitted." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
