<urn:usf:requirement:completion-check-receipts-pending-publication-snapshot:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Extract one private authenticated scalar receipt-publication snapshot shared by native receipt recovery and the named canonical recovery reader. It may classify only absent, final singleton, pending singleton, or exact final-pending hardlink publication after no-follow ancestry, file identity, ownership, mode, link-count, byte, receipt binding and authority checks, plus full rederived current candidate, basis, validation, runtime-authority dependency and receipt-claim authentication. The named recovery reader authenticates pending and hardlinked publication without mutation but reports them recoverable-not-current; validation receipt sets, evidence, completion and terminal paths may not project them as current members. STARTED with a fully current pending or hardlinked snapshot remains STARTED and reconciliation-required, never UNKNOWN; SETTLED requires a final singleton. Before native link or unlink, reauthenticate the shared snapshot and require exact before and after candidate, basis, validation, runtime-authority, receipt byte and file identity equality. The existing native recovery alone links or unlinks and fsyncs before strict final readback. The public strict reader preserves its existing pending and hardlink refusal. Unsafe, conflicting, stale or changed snapshots preserve bytes and refuse. No new schema, stored state, controller, adapter, provider, completion or parallel authority is introduced." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
