<urn:usf:contract:cli-transition-definition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "The separately required pending receipt-publication snapshot repair may modify only the existing scalar receipt publication and recovery composition in src/commands/check.ts, existing compiled-rule fingerprint compatibility in src/commands/transition.ts, canonical receipt-set observation in src/commands/work-completion.ts, and focused interruption/root regressions. It must share one authenticated publication snapshot between native mutation and named read-only recovery, preserve the ordinary strict receipt reader, update the existing compiled-rule fingerprint compatibility for the amended rule text, and never project pending or hardlinked publication as a current receipt, receipt-set result, evidence, completion or terminal state. It may add no receipt schema or stored state, controller, adapter, lock policy, provider contact, proof, publication or parallel authority." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-definition> .
